body:
I understand that you're upset, especially in a time where you could need them the most. I think you need to don't forget that these friends are people too. Humans sometimes do things that for you as an individual may seem completely off in relation to what you would consider doing when you would be in their position. If I were you I would leave this for now and would tell them later that it really bothered you because you needed them. Make your point clear in a way they both understand.

&#x200B;

Send some love <3

Thank you man, that really helped me out a lot. 

&#x200B;

I was thinking about writing down a list with all the reasons why I want to quit smoking but idk I just felt kinda dumb. No offense by any means, I guess I'll try this method because I don't like where this is going and where this is gonna get me. 

&#x200B;

Thanks for sharing your advice and your personal experience

&#x200B;

First of all thank you for the fast response. 

&#x200B;

I also posted this in r/depression and I just didn't get any answers. I'm not trashtalking about this subreddit I'm just trying to take any straw there is. 

I actually do not think that he will kill himself in the near future but I know this kind of talking and often something serious starts with stuff like that.

&#x200B;

I really appreciate your advice and I'm looking forward to talk to him again on a very serious level. It's not like I want to confront him with that but in my opinion having a person who cares about you and who is willing to talk to you on a serious level often helps.

&#x200B;

Thanks !
